      "reasoning": "The student recognizes the need for the quadratic formula and notes a specific pain point with the negative coefficient of x (-1). I should validate this common hurdle, give them the formula, and ask them to identify $a$, $b$, and $c$. [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"(1 + 181**0.5) / 10\") -> 1.4462]",
      "content": "Dealing with negative signs can definitely be tricky, but writing out the brackets carefully will keep us safe!\n\nThe quadratic formula is:\n$$x = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}$|\n\nBased on your equation $5x^2 - x - 9 = 0$, what are the values of $a$, $b$, and $c$?"
