      "role": "assistant",
      "reasoning": "The student correctly identified a=5, b=-1, c=-9 and asked a smart question about substituting -(-1). I will confirm their question, show the substitution step, and ask them to compute the discriminant under the square root. [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"(1 - 181**0.5) / 10\") -> -1.2462]",
      "content": "Yes, exactly! Because the formula has a negative $b$ (written as $-b$) and your $b$ value is already negative ($-1$), it becomes $-(-1)$, which turns into a positive $1$.\n\nYour substitution looks like this:\n$$x = \\frac{-(-1) \\pm \\sqrt{(-1)^2 - 4(5)(-9)}}{2(5)}$$\n\nCan you calculate the value inside the square root (the discriminant, $b^2 - 4ac$)?"
